{"columns":["notice_id","section_id","field_id","ordinal","value"],"row_count":25,"rows":[[46792127,"1","BT-24-Lot",0,"Provision of External Audit Services"],[46792127,"PROCEDURE","BT-24-Procedure",0,"Provision of External Audit Services"],[46813997,"1","BT-24-Lot",0,"Central East ICB, previously Cambridgeshire and Peterborough ICB are intending to award a contract to an existing provider following direct award process C for a duration of 36 months, from 01/04/2026 - 31/03/2029.\nThe financial values included are indicative and subject to final approval. The indicative annual value of the contract is £24,759. Additional information: There are anticipated system "],[46813997,"PROCEDURE","BT-24-Procedure",0,"Bereavement support within Cambridgeshire and Peterborough"],[46869034,"1","BT-24-Lot",0,"Provision of bereavement counselling for people registered with a GP in Birmingham/Solihull"],[46869034,"PROCEDURE","BT-24-Procedure",0,"This is a Provider Selection Regime (PSR) intention to award notice. The awarding of this contract is subject to the Health Care Services (Provider Selection Regime) Regulations 2023. For the avoidance of doubt, the provisions of the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 do not apply to this award. The publication of this notice marks the start of the standstill period. Representations by providers mu"],[46877907,"1","BT-24-Lot",0,"The award of a contract relating to Mental Health Crisis Text Messaging Service; this notice is an intention to award a contract under the most suitable provider process, for a 12 month period at a cost of £162,000 per annum.\nThis is a new service and the intention is to award to Mental Health Innovations, a new provider with BSMHFT"],[46877907,"PROCEDURE","BT-24-Procedure",0,"The  crisis text service is defined by the comprehensive approach to supporting everyone in mental health crisis, irrespective of their background and demographics. The clinically led service aims to provide timely, accessible, and effective support including a range of interventions tailored to meet the diverse needs of service users in Birmingham and Solihull."],[46898329,"1","BT-24-Lot",0,"Select Catering Consultancy are assisting Town & Country Housing with the facilitation of this tender process.  If you have any queries please email philchivers@selectcateringconsultancy.co.uk. Additional information: Bidder site visits will take place on the 20th/21st/22nd August - details are provided in the tender documents and bidders are requested to advise Phil Chivers, via email philchivers"],[46898329,"PROCEDURE","BT-24-Procedure",0,"Town & Country Housing provide more than 13,000 affordable homes in 15 local authority areas in Kent, Surrey and Sussex. Over the years they have invested heavily in their homes. In addition to general needs homes, Town & Country Housing offer a wide range of housing, including key worker, shared ownership and specialist accommodation.\nTown & Country Housing undertaking this tender process with th"],[46935105,"1","BT-24-Lot",0,"Care Navigator Service \nContract to be awarded to existing supplier under PSR Direct Award C process. 2 year\ncontract plus 2 x 6 month extension."],[46935105,"PROCEDURE","BT-24-Procedure",0,"A significant number of patients in East Kent are currently accessing accident and emergency for conditions that could be treated locally in the community. The health and social care economy in East Kent believe that aligning provider services in an integrated approach and underpinning this with a redirection programme will reduce pressure on hospital services and improve overall performance acros"],[46938925,"1","BT-24-Lot",0,"Community Based Recovery Service for People with Mental Ill Health delivered in individual dispersed properties."],[46938925,"10","BT-24-Lot",0,"Supported Accommodation Service for Single Vulnerable Young People"],[46938925,"2","BT-24-Lot",0,"Supported Accommodation Service for People with Mental Ill Health"],[46938925,"3","BT-24-Lot",0,"Supported Accommodation Service for People with Mental Ill Health"],[46938925,"4","BT-24-Lot",0,"Community Based Recovery Service for People with Mental Ill Health"],[46938925,"5","BT-24-Lot",0,"Supported Accommodation and Outreach for Single Socially Excluded People"],[46938925,"6","BT-24-Lot",0,"Supported Accommodation for Single Homes People"],[46938925,"7","BT-24-Lot",0,"Community Based Housing Related Support and Homeless Prevention Services for Young People"],[46938925,"8","BT-24-Lot",0,"Supported Accommodation and Outreach based Service for Young People"],[46938925,"9","BT-24-Lot",0,"Supported Accommodation Service for Teenage Parents"],[46938925,"PROCEDURE","BT-24-Procedure",0,"Housing related support services including supported accommodation and community based outreach for vulnerable homeless people or those at risk of homelessness."],[46976243,"1","BT-24-Lot",0,"In order to assist with the tech transfer from Catapult the following items are being purchased are to be purchased asap:\n1 x Sartorius Biowelder\n1 x Sartorius Biosealer\n1 x Sartorius BIOSTAT® RM 20 / 50 (BIOSTAT® B - perfusion ready)\n1 x Sartorius Twin UniVessel 2 L STR + BIOSTAT® B\nBetween 2022 and 2027 the following items may be purchased:-\n2 x Sartorius Biowelder\n2 x Sartorius Biosealer\n2 x Sa"],[46976243,"PROCEDURE","BT-24-Procedure",0,"The University of Sheffield (UoS) is establishing a new 'Gene Therapy Innovation Manufacturing Centre' (GTIMC) to advance scientific discoveries into life-changing treatments for patients with life threatening diseases. The Sheffield GTIMC  will be one of three cutting edge hubs in the UK dedicated to advancing the clinical development  of new genetic treatments. This facility is due to open in th"]],"truncated":false}